LRC(14) SDP tooling (cvxpy 1.9.2, SCS+CLARABEL) -- moment-SOS for M(S)=max_t min_v ||vt||
via univariate Chebyshev: c=cos(2 pi t), sin^2(pi v t)=(1-T_v(c))/2, M(S)=arcsin(sqrt(M~))/pi.
VALIDATED EXACTLY: S={1,2,3} -> M~=0.5 => M=1/4; S={1,2,4} -> M~=0.75 => M=1/3.
NUMERICAL LIMITS (free solvers): moment relaxation tight but SCS inaccurate on rank-deficient optima
(non-monotone in R); SOS dual single-solve but slow convergence (loose for {1,2,3},{1,2,3,4}).
Would need MOSEK for scale. NOTE: M(S) is exactly computable by rational sweep -- the SDP adds only the
magic-function certificate, not the value. The LRC endgame SDP target is p0/L_y (THM-534), not M(S).
